# etude-pqv verify gate

ROLE: Review the VERIFY phase for etude-pqv against its accepted behavior and scope.

ANCESTOR: etude-pqv (P3, urgent dependency of etude-9uf) replaces an observed nested-Claude HTTP 401 comment-only exception with an executable registry contract and ensures `etude init --force` does not regenerate stale seat behavior.

MEASUREMENT: before this change the checked-in registry differed from `registry.Default()` across four seats/settings, and `claude -p` is observed to return 401 when Claude Code is the outer orchestrator.

BLAST RADIUS: none: repository and private `/tmp` verification repo only. No external writes, installs, shared-state mutation, or forbidden 9uf-owned files.

IRREVERSIBLE SEQUENCES: none

TOPOLOGY: single-process parse, encode, and ordered candidate enumeration. No new concurrent writer.

DURABILITY CLASS: Git-tracked registry YAML and compiled scaffold defaults are durable. Enumeration is read-only and consumer retry is outside this bead.

COMPLETENESS ENUMERATION: registry schema, validation, strict decode, encode, defaults, checked-in registry, ordered enumeration, legacy omission, exact golden, migration equality, CLI regeneration, generated docs, and hand-written docs reality were all checked.

TRUST BOUNDARY: registry YAML remains trusted operator-authored configuration parsed with unknown-field rejection. The engine does not use ambient environment to infer an orchestrator.

